<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#urdu">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urdu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urdu is an Indo-Aryan language closely related to Hindi, written in a Perso-Arabic script and rich in Persian and Arabic vocabulary. It developed in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from the interaction of local speech with the Persian of the ruling elites. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> cite the development of Urdu, together with Indo-Persian traditions, as part of the empire's enduring linguistic and cultural legacy.</p></div>
